# Test database isolation

Tests and smoke runs MUST NOT write to the production Neon database (the one
the Vercel viewer and the Modal skills read/write).

- Never INSERT into live tables (`skill_edit_proposals`, `skill_lineage`,
  `forecasts`, `forecasts_shadow`, `signals`, `evaluations`) from a test.
- Use one of: a separate test `DATABASE_URL`; a transaction rolled back in
  teardown; or capture every inserted id and delete it in teardown.
- A passing test must leave the database exactly as it found it. The operator
  approval queue is production state — never seed it with fixtures.
